        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">In (your n)ame, Merci(ful One).</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">The letter of his excellency, the most illustrio[us] elder, has arrived.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[It was] the most gladdening [letter that has come] and the most delightf[ul] missive to arrive. I read it with joy, pondered it [happy and pleased], and understood it.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">News of his well-being and good condition gladdened me, and I praised G[od, e]xalted be He, grea[tly] for it.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">I asked Him to grant [him] more of every good,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">by His mercy, God willing. My lord the most illustrious elder has described no longing that your excellency&rsquo;s servant does not feel many times over.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[I ask] God [to make] his honor [last] and to ease a reunion between me and him in the</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">happiest circumstances and with the most contented mind, by His grace and generosity, God willing. My lord mentioned</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">that he was held up this year for various reasons, and also because of the high price of cloth (bazz). Perhaps it is for the best; may God,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">exalted be He, choose what is best for him. No doubt the chief cause of the delay was none other</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">than Shaykh Is\u1e25\u0101q al-Naf\u016bs\u012b. As for the cloth, had he bought it at any price, however high,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">it would have been a great profit. This year in Aden the bleached (maq\u1e63\u016br) [cloth]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">sold at a market price of two dinars &hellip; the unbleached (kh\u0101m) &hellip;</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">22 dinars per bale (khurja). There was a tremendous demand for cloth. He mentioned [...]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">and it was slack (k\u0101sid), and that he was upset about it. My lord the [most illustrious] elder,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">may God not deprive me of your kindness, do not take it to heart. Let it be sold for a dirham or anything else, and kindly</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">buy with the proceeds a small quantity of musk pods (n\u0101fija) or good loose musk (misk nathr). As for the khum\u0101siyy\u0101t (&ldquo;fives&rdquo;),</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">my lord should not buy any of them, either for himself or for anyone else. They are worth nothing in</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Fustat, or in Aden either.&nbsp;The bale of ma\u1e25\u0101bis&nbsp;that my lords kindly</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">bought has arrived. May God not deprive my lord of beneficence, as he has always been.&nbsp;By God, my lord,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">we missed you this year,&nbsp; and his delay was hard on his servant. But there was</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">nothing my lord could do. May God choose what is best for him and bring it to a good</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">end. My most illustrious lord mentioned the small item of his held by the elder Ab\u016b Sa\u02bf\u012bd</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">b. Ma\u1e25f\u016b\u1e93, and that the elder Khalaf&nbsp; b. Yi\u1e63\u1e25aq should take delivery of it. This year the elder&nbsp;</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Ab\u016b Sa\u02bf\u012bd arrived from India after a good journey. He handed over what belonged to the excellency of my lord</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">to the elder&nbsp;Khalaf b. Yi\u1e63\u1e25aq, and it passed into his possession. Pepper had a good market: we sold each</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">bah\u0101r of pepper for thirty-eight dinars and a little better. As for the elder&nbsp;Khalaf,</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">your servant does not know at what price he sold his excellency&rsquo;s goods. Also, what belonged to his excellency of the cloth arrived with the elder Barak\u0101t</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">al-\u1e24alab\u012b, as my lord described in his letter,</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
